Here is a PowerShell one-liner that attempts to create a socket connection to 203.0.113.5 on port 8080 and outputs whether it succeeded:

```powershell
try {
  $tcpClient = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient
  $tcpClient.Connect("203.0.113.5", 8080)
  Write-Output "Connection succeeded"
  $tcpClient.Close()
} catch {
  Write-Output "Connection failed: $_"
}
```

This script tries to connect and prints a success message or failure reason accordingly.

